WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.978
Every scan, a tracker must decide which new plot belongs to which track.

2
00:00:05.028 --> 00:00:11.192
The dashed circles show where each track expects its target, one standard deviation wide.

3
00:00:11.842 --> 00:00:16.003
Greedy nearest neighbour serves the tracks one at a time.

4
00:00:16.053 --> 00:00:23.169
Track one takes its closest plot, which leaves track two with a plot far outside its expectation.

5
00:00:23.219 --> 00:00:25.754
The total statistical cost is 13.3.

6
00:00:26.404 --> 00:00:36.036
Global nearest neighbour solves every pairing at once, with the Hungarian algorithm, and picks the set with the lowest total cost, 3.7 here.

7
00:00:36.086 --> 00:00:38.249
Each track keeps its own target.

8
00:00:38.299 --> 00:00:42.121
This is the one-to-one matching in the learning roadmap.
